  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2002-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(15^2+20^2=225+400\\) \\(=625=25^2,\\) the triangle is right with legs \\(15\\) and \\(20,\\) and area \\(\\dfrac{1}{2}(15)(20)=150.\\)\n\nThe shortest altitude falls to the longest side \\(25,\\) and equals \\(\\dfrac{2\\cdot 150}{25}=12.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Check whether \\(15,\\) \\(20,\\) \\(25\\) is a right triangle",
        "The shortest altitude is drawn to the longest side"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
